@startuml
title Beacon-Guided Air Valve Game - Main FSM

[*] --> INIT

INIT --> NAVIGATION : set route START_TO_EXPERIENCE

NAVIGATION --> EXPERIENCE_MISSION : target found + ENTER\nnextState = EXPERIENCE_MISSION

EXPERIENCE_MISSION --> NAVIGATION : mission question correct\nset route EXPERIENCE_TO_MATERIAL_QUESTION

NAVIGATION --> MATERIAL_QUESTION : target found + ENTER\nnextState = MATERIAL_QUESTION

MATERIAL_QUESTION --> NAVIGATION : required parts answer correct\nset route MATERIAL_QUESTION_TO_COLLECTION

NAVIGATION --> MATERIAL_COLLECTION : target found + ENTER\nnextState = MATERIAL_COLLECTION

MATERIAL_COLLECTION --> NAVIGATION : checksum correct\nset route COLLECTION_TO_BUILD_TEST

NAVIGATION --> BUILD_AND_TEST : target found + ENTER\nnextState = BUILD_AND_TEST

BUILD_AND_TEST --> NAVIGATION : valve test passed\nset route BUILD_TEST_TO_FINISH

NAVIGATION --> FINISH : target found + ENTER\nnextState = FINISH

FINISH --> SUCCESS : mission complete
SUCCESS --> [*]

note right of NAVIGATION
Generic navigation state.

It does not know fixed room names.
It uses the active RouteProfile
to interpret beacon IDs.

Same beacon can be:
- PASS_BY in one route
- TARGET in another route
- WRONG_WAY in another route
end note
note bottom
Design rule:

Mission states handle puzzles.
Navigation state handles movement between locations.

Do not mix beacon logic into mission states.
end note

@enduml